Let $p>5$ be a prime and let $\left(\tfrac{\cdot}{p}\right)$ denote the Legendre symbol. Define the polynomial sequence
$$T_n := \sum_{k=0}^{n}\binom{n}{k}\binom{n+2k}{2k}\binom{2k}{k}(-324)^{n-k}\qquad(n\ge 0).$$
Prove or disprove the following statements.

(1) One has the congruence
$$\sum_{n=0}^{p-1}\frac{357n+103}{2160^{n}}\binom{2n}{n}T_n\;\equiv\; p\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)\!\left(54+49\left(\tfrac{105}{p}\right)\right)\pmod{p^2}.$$

(2) One has
$$\sum_{n=0}^{p-1}\frac{\binom{2n}{n}}{2160^{n}}T_n\;\equiv\; R(p)\pmod{p^2},$$
where $R(p)$ is determined by the residues of $p$ as follows (with $x,y\in\mathbb{Z}$ in each case):

• $4x^2-2p$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=1$ and $p=x^2+105y^2$;
• $2x^2-2p$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=1$, $\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=-1$, and $2p=x^2+105y^2$;
• $2p-12x^2$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=-1$ and $p=3x^2+35y^2$;
• $2p-6x^2$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=-1$, $\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=1$, and $2p=3x^2+35y^2$;
• $20x^2-2p$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=1$, $\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=-1$, and $p=5x^2+21y^2$;
• $10x^2-2p$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=1$, $\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=-1$, and $2p=5x^2+21y^2$;
• $28x^2-2p$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=-1$, $\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=1$, and $p=7x^2+15y^2$;
• $14x^2-2p$ if $\left(\tfrac{-1}{p}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{3}\right)=-1$, $\left(\tfrac{p}{5}\right)=\left(\tfrac{p}{7}\right)=1$, and $2p=7x^2+15y^2$;
• $0$ if $\left(\tfrac{-105}{p}\right)=-1$.

(3) The series identity
$$\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{357n+103}{2160^{n}}\binom{2n}{n}T_n=\frac{90}{\pi}$$
holds.

